### fix(security): apply receipt-circuit cleanup to the deployed in-package tree + pin .circom source sync

- `receipt_simple.circom`: the dead `BidRangeProof` removal now also applied to the in-package copy the service actually loads (`apps/coordinator-api/.../zk-circuits/`); recompiled r1cs is byte-identical to the committed artifact (`6a873d…`), so deployed zkeys/vkeys are unaffected.
- `scripts/ci/check-zk-circuit-sync.sh` + pre-commit hook: the two circuit trees (build workspace vs deployed package) must keep identical `.circom` sources; artifacts may differ (separate ceremonies).
- `audit-findings.md`: receipt finding status now `Resolved (closed by architecture)`; old remediation marked superseded; `data_layer`/`stage_runner` findings marked Resolved (fixed in 05fd6c206b). Ledger-wide consistency check finds no status/note disagreements.

### fix(security): generic /zk/verify refuses receipt circuits; agent-integration ZK mock gated

- `POST /verify` returned `verified` for caller-supplied signals — valid for the signals given, not evidence of correct computation. Receipt circuits (`receipt_model`/`receipt_public`/`receipt_simple`) now get 400 pointing at `/receipt/verify`, which binds proofs to server-derived signals. Docstring states the semantics plainly.
- `agent_coordination` mock `ZKProofService` (fake proof ids, always `verified: true`) was reachable via the mounted admin router `/v1/agents/integration/integrations/zk/{id}`. Its methods now raise unless `AGENT_INTEGRATION_ZK_MOCK=1` (dev only); the integration flow records the failures non-fatally in `integration_errors`.

### fix(security): ML verify docstrings, ZK-mock flag surfaced, endpoint 503

- `/v1/ml-zk/verify/training` and `/verify/inference`: docstrings now state `verified` = validity for caller-supplied signals only (no in-repo consumer treats them as acceptance — wording fix, no refusal needed).
- `AGENT_INTEGRATION_ZK_MOCK` documented in ENVIRONMENT_CONFIGURATION.md (dangerous-if-set); `fleet-config-check.sh` flags it in env files or the running coordinator process.
- `POST /v1/agents/integration/integrations/zk/{id}` returns a clear 503 while the mock is disabled instead of recording mock-verification failures.

### fix(security): dev-flag checks fail the fleet-config gate

- `AGENT_INTEGRATION_ZK_MOCK` set on any host now fails `fleet-config-check.sh` (was report-only) — a fake `verified` should not hide in long output.
- Same for `SYNC_VALIDATE_SIGNATURES_SKIP_UNTIL`: a live signature kill-switch is silent consensus weakening and now fails the gate too.

### fix(fleet-check): three check bugs surfaced by flag verification

- `running_env` died under `set -u` for 3-arg calls (`grep$4` unbound) — now `${4:-}`.
- Changelog-coverage `cat` died under `set -e` when the top-level `*_change.log` glob misses — now `|| true`.
- Same section reported every covered commit uncovered: `echo "$LOG_FILES" | grep -qF` loses to SIGPIPE under `pipefail` — now a pure-bash `case` match.
- `skip_flagged`/`mock_flagged`/`height_bad` initialized at top with the other accumulators — a skipped section must never look like a clean one.

### fix(bridge): verdict split + alert throttle + check-bug fixes

- `fleet-config-check.sh`: new `v9-pin-gate:` verdict line reads only the consensus/pin subset (env drift, heights, kill-switch, mock flag, v9 window, validators, gossip, digests, convergence) — bridge monitor alerts and doc hygiene still redden the overall verdict but cannot block the pin. Full-roster note added to the header; `v9_bad` initialized with the other accumulators.
- `bridge_monitor`: low-float alerts were emitted every poll while the condition held — now throttled to once per `BRIDGE_FLOAT_ALERT_INTERVAL_SECONDS` (default 3600) per condition, re-alerting immediately on a fresh episode.
- Deposit ledger: the `58acfadb` "no recipient" row was the operator float top-up, already `written_off`. `746aebaf` (0.05 ETH from `0x42645cE4`, no memo, failed since Sep 26) remains open — needs an operator refund/write-off decision.
